      "content": "i hear you, but it feels like you're saying there's only one \"right\" way to plan a city. if a board member argues that moving goods and people via highways is essential for the immediate economic survival of suburban businesses, isn't that a legitimate economic argument rather than just an \"outdated mindset\"? can you explain why the transit side is objectively better for the economy in the long run without just calling the other side outdated?",
